course: dictionary
lesson: 14116
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use the context to find the right one. Look at the words around the word, and ask what would make sense here.
explain: «The kitten mews at the door.» A kitten cannot be a street or a house, so mews here is a sound: the kitten makes a soft crying noise. «We live in a mews house.» Here mews is a kind of house, so it is a noun.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Mews is a noun and a verb. As a noun, one mews and many mews look the same.
fact: «Mews» (UK) means a row of old stables in a small street or yard, often now turned into houses or flats.
fact: The little street itself can also be called a mews, as in «Ivy Mews».
fact: «Mews» (verb) means a cat makes a soft crying sound, as in «the kitten mews» when it is hungry or lonely.
fact: Long ago, a mews was also a building where hunting hawks were kept while they moulted.
exercise: «The kitten mews at the door, asking for its tea.» What does mews mean here? | It runs fast down the street | It climbs the tallest tree | * It makes a soft crying sound | It sleeps all day in a box
exercise: «We live in a mews house in the middle of the city.» What is a mews house? | A tall tower with a bell | * A house made from old stables, often in a small street | A house with no doors at all | A house built on a boat
exercise: «The sign at the end of the lane said Ivy Mews.» What does Mews mean in this sentence? | A soft crying sound made by a cat | A kind of cake | A bird that hunts mice | * The name of a small street
test: «The old stables behind the big house were turned into a mews of cosy homes.» What is a mews in this sentence? | A street with no houses | A place where hawks are kept while they moult | A type of car park | A cat's soft cry | * A row of old stables turned into houses
test: «The little cat mews softly under the table.» What is the cat doing? | Building a nest in a tree | Sleeping in a box | Chasing a mouse across the floor | * Making a soft crying sound
exam: In «Mia's cat mews at the door of her mews house», which meaning fits the second mews? | A soft crying sound made by a cat | * A row of old stables turned into houses | A large bird that hunts | A kind of sweet bread
